<!--
  Android user copy.

  This file did not exist before: every string on this frontend was a Kotlin
  literal, which is why the Android UI was the one place in the project that
  could only ever be read in English. `scripts/check-i18n.sh` covers the
  HarmonyOS tables; this is the Android half of the same rule, and
  `apps/android/TODO.md` records the copy that has not been migrated yet.

  These are the strings the chat top bar and the settings pages need. They are
  named for what they say, not for where they sit, so a label can move between
  surfaces without being renamed.
-->
